  └─────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  The last two are the progressive-enhancement contract: [1mthe in-page panel is the source of truth, and the OS toast is [0m
  [1mnever load-bearing.[0m Nothing is reachable only via toast.

  [1mTesting (Vitest, unit only).[0m The milestone matrix as a table: no due date, far future, exactly at [38;5;153mdueAt - 24h[39m, inside
  the window, exactly at [38;5;153mdueAt[39m, past due, completed-but-overdue, already acknowledged, garbage date. The two
  exact-boundary cases pin the inclusive/exclusive edges, which is where this kind of logic actually breaks. Plus
  [38;5;153mdiffNew[39m, and the storage modules against a fake localStorage.

  Deliberately untested: DOM rendering and the Notifications API. That's the direct consequence of skipping e2e — so
  those layers stay thin and decision-free, pushing anything worth asserting down into the pure modules. I'd rather say
  that plainly now than have it discovered later as a coverage gap.

